{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T00:17:55.466Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"4be2fd7d6f19dab50a5a483b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-26T00:17:55.466Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Pack verification: npm pack --dry-run --json and the actual npm pack --ignore-scripts artifact agree on 216 allowlisted files (dist: 164; docs: 28; examples: 17; root files: 7). Every packed member was scanned for absolute home paths, npm/GitHub/cloud tokens, private keys, hosted-data locations, private addresses and historical owner email addresses: PASS with zero matches. Regression proof: five independent workflow mutations (approval, provenance, token environment, daily schedule and OR bypass) plus the original manifest each fail the new contract check; restored contract passes 4/4. The linked test also passes through pm test --run --progress. Next gates: npm run release:check and bun run release:check with isolated HOME and Git configuration."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T00:17:55.466Z"}],"before_hash":"0a8b8188afc21b650508cf2b3b0e59efd20c7f189ce3b9967313054601ab4908","after_hash":"8a1c5d88bd2f3e7df12c461b13cff8b9169e674db768122f551803021a4423b4","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"59df84db18a297cb33c478fbcc7e5c84b2aacae583f67bc1e4b1f6ec93dab